      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset_Beach%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sunset Beach’s low-lying terrain averages 3 to 10 feet above sea level, making it vulnerable to tidal influences and coastal processes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Sunset_Beach,_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic water tower, dating to the late 19th-century rail era, stands as a landmark of Sunset Beach’s early transportation history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Sunset_Beach,_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sunset Beach’s surf culture attracts enthusiasts for body surfing, kitesurfing, and board sports, supported by nearby rental spots like OEX Sunset Beach and Huntington Surf & Sport.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
